    {
      "page_title": "Unbuffered Channels: Rendezvous",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Signal Channel",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "done := make(chan struct{}) // 0 bytes",
            "close(done) // wakes every receiver"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Rendezvous, Not Queue",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Unbuffered means a synchronous handoff",
            "Sender and receiver must both arrive first",
            "No value is ever placed inside the channel",
            "It copies straight to the receiver's stack slot"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Classic Deadlock",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "func main() {",
            "\tch := make(chan int)",
            "\tch <- 1 // no receiver, ever",
            "}",
            "// fatal error: all goroutines asleep"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Send then receive in one goroutine self-deadlocks",
            "The send blocks even if a receiver is about to arrive",
            "No speculative buffering, no grace period"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What You Get For It",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Spec: a send happens before its receive completes",
            "So it is a synchronization primitive, not a queue",
            "After `ch <- v` returns, a receiver holds `v`",
            "Backpressure is total: slow consumer throttles producer"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Standard Uses",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "go func() { work(); done <- struct{}{} }()",
            "<-done // completion signal, exact"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Ping-pong: two goroutines alternating turns",
            "Lockstep needs the rendezvous; a buffer breaks it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Price Per Handoff",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Operation",
            "Cost"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "unbuffered handoff",
              "~100ns+"
            ],
            [
              "atomic add",
              "~10ns"
            ],
            [
              "why",
              "park + reschedule"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Rule Of Thumb",
          "text": "Start unbuffered. Add a buffer only when you can say the reason out loud in one sentence."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Ring Buffer Inside",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "jobs := make(chan int, 3) // FIFO ring",
            "jobs <- 1 // len 1, cap 3",
            "jobs <- 2 // len 2, still no receiver"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "array",
          "spec": {
            "cells": [
              "job 1",
              "job 2",
              "empty"
            ],
            "indices": true,
            "pointers": [],
            "highlight": [],
            "dim": [],
            "caption": "hchan buf, cap 3"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Buffered Channels: Sizing The Queue",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Send blocks only when the buffer is full",
            "Receive blocks only when it is empty",
            "Sender may run ahead by up to `cap` items",
            "A finished send says nothing about receipt"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Semaphore Pattern",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "sem := make(chan struct{}, 10)",
            "sem <- struct{}{}        // acquire",
            "defer func() { <-sem }() // release"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A buffer of N caps in-flight work at N",
            "That N is your memory ceiling, so pick it",
            "`len(ch)` and `cap(ch)` are racy for decisions",
            "The value can change before the next line runs"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Capacity One",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "sig := make(chan os.Signal, 1)",
            "signal.Notify(sig, os.Interrupt) // no block"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`signal.Notify` never blocks, so it needs the slot",
            "Cap 1 also breaks a send/receive lockstep",
            "Producer and consumer then overlap by one item"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Choosing A Size",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Trait",
            "Unbuffered",
            "Buffered"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "timing",
              "sync",
              "async to cap"
            ],
            [
              "guarantee",
              "strong",
              "weak"
            ],
            [
              "backpressure",
              "instant",
              "deferred"
            ],
            [
              "switches",
              "more",
              "fewer"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Buffering smooths bursts, adds queueing delay",
            "It also delays failure detection downstream",
            "An oversized buffer hides a slow consumer until OOM"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "The Anti-Pattern",
          "text": "Sizing the buffer to the number of items so you never block is an unbounded queue wearing a channel costume."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Also `qcount`, `dataqsiz`, `sendx`, `recvx`",
            "Every operation takes `hchan.lock` first",
            "That is a runtime mutex, not a `sync.Mutex`",
            "Wait queues hold `sudog` records wrapping goroutines"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Inside The Runtime: hchan",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Struct",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "type hchan struct {",
            "\tbuf unsafe.Pointer // ring array",
            "\tsendq, recvq waitq // parked gs",
            "\tlock mutex // runtime, not sync",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Fast Path",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "sender arrives",
              "receiver in `recvq`",
              "copy to its stack",
              "buffer skipped"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Direct handoff is why unbuffered needs no buffer",
            "A buffered channel with a waiting receiver acts unbuffered"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Park And Ready",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Event",
            "Runtime",
            "Cost"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "block",
              "`gopark`",
              "M freed"
            ],
            [
              "wake",
              "`goready`",
              "requeued"
            ],
            [
              "no park",
              "fast path",
              "tens of ns"
            ],
            [
              "park+wake",
              "scheduler",
              "hundreds of ns"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Blocking is goroutine-blocking, not thread-blocking",
            "100k blocked goroutines cost KB, not OS threads",
            "Queues are FIFO: arrival order, no starvation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Memory And Copies",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`make(chan T, n)` is one block: header plus `n*sizeof(T)`",
            "Through the buffer a value is copied twice: in, then out",
            "On the ==direct-handoff== fast path it is copied once",
            "Either way a large struct is `memmove`'d, so send a pointer"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Ownership Is Convention",
          "text": "Sending a pointer transfers ownership by agreement only. The runtime will not stop you touching it afterwards, but `-race` will."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Why select Is Safe",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "`select` locks every involved channel in address order. Two selects over the same pair therefore cannot deadlock against each other."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "v, ok := <-ch // ok=false: closed+drained",
            "for v := range ch { use(v) } // idiomatic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A send on a closed channel panics, never errors",
            "There is no try-close and no error-returning form"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Closer Pattern",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "for _, p := range prods { go p.run(out) }",
            "go func() { wg.Wait(); close(out) }()",
            "for v := range out { collect(v) }"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Closing Channels",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What close Does",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`close(ch)` marks it closed; it frees nothing",
            "Buffered values survive: receivers drain them first",
            "Then receives return the zero value forever",
            "A receive on a closed channel never blocks"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Three Panics",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Action",
            "Result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "send on closed",
              "panic"
            ],
            [
              "close of closed",
              "panic"
            ],
            [
              "close of nil",
              "panic"
            ],
            [
              "receive on closed",
              "zero value"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Who Closes",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "The Rule",
          "text": "Only the sender closes, and only when there is exactly one sender. A receiver must never close a channel."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Multiple senders? Do not close from a sender at all",
            "Use a separate `done` channel, or a `sync.Once`",
            "Or a `WaitGroup` plus one dedicated closer goroutine"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Close is a broadcast: it wakes every blocked receiver",
            "That is how one `done` cancels N workers at once",
            "You need not close every channel; GC collects it",
            "Close only to signal that no more data is coming"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Zero-Value Trap",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A sender may legitimately send the zero value",
            "A bare `v := <-ch` cannot tell that from a close",
            "`v, ok := <-ch` is the only distinguisher"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Live Trap",
          "items": [
            "`close(results)` before workers finish sending",
            "Next worker send: `panic: send on closed channel`",
            "A panic in a goroutine kills the whole process"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Waiting On Many",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "select {",
            "case v := <-a: use(v)",
            "case b <- x: sent()",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "default Is Non-Blocking",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "select {",
            "case v := <-ch: use(v) // got one",
            "default: // nothing ready, move on",
            "}"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "select: Multiplexing",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Every case must be a channel operation",
            "It proceeds with whichever op is ready first",
            "Several ready? It picks one uniformly at random",
            "Random choice, not top-down, so no case starves"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Timeout And Cancel",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "select {",
            "case r := <-work: return r",
            "case <-time.After(2 * time.Second):",
            "\treturn ErrTimeout // fires once",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Pre-1.23: `time.After` kept its timer alive until it fired",
            "In a hot loop those timers piled up",
            "==Go 1.23+== collects unreferenced timers at once: leak gone",
            "Still prefer `time.NewTimer` + `defer t.Stop()` to cancel early",
            "`case <-ctx.Done(): return ctx.Err()` in every worker"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Blocking Forever",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Form",
            "Behaviour"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`select {}`",
              "parks this goroutine"
            ],
            [
              "nil cases, no default",
              "same as `select {}`"
            ],
            [
              "every goroutine parked",
              "fatal deadlock"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Cases are evaluated before the select blocks",
            "Channel expressions and send operands run exactly once",
            "They are computed top to bottom, then it waits"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Event Loop",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "select { // wrap this in for { }",
            "case j := <-jobs: handle(j)",
            "case <-ctx.Done(): return",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Guard Every Send",
          "text": "`for { select { ... } }` is the shape of most Go services. An unguarded `out <- v` inside one is the number one source of goroutine leaks."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Never-Made Channel",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "var ch chan int // nil, never made",
            "ch <- 1   // blocks forever",
            "<-ch      // blocks forever",
            "close(ch) // panic: close of nil chan"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Alone in a goroutine that is a plain deadlock",
            "Inside a `select` the same behaviour is a feature",
            "A case on a nil channel is never chosen: disabled"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "nil Channels: The Off Switch",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Disable A Case",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Set the variable to nil once its stream is exhausted",
            "`select` stops considering that case from then on",
            "Loop while `a != nil || b != nil` to know you are done",
            "Both nil means every input drained, so exit"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Busy-Spin Bug",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "select {",
            "case v, ok := <-a: use(v, ok) // spins",
            "case v, ok := <-b: use(v, ok)",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "After `a` closes, its case fires on every iteration",
            "`ok == false` each time, burning a core at full speed"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Fix",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "select {",
            "case v, ok := <-a:",
            "\tif !ok { a = nil; continue } // drop out",
            "\tuse(v)",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "nil vs closed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "nil channel",
                "lines": [
                  "send blocks forever",
                  "receive blocks forever",
                  "invisible to select",
                  "close panics"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "closed channel",
                "lines": [
                  "send panics",
                  "receive returns zero",
